d reference Agent 1's point and add our perspective.\n\nWe have candidate facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, pretentious, wrong tone. Also B has weak memory for numbers (from notes). That could affect attention and information accuracy. That is a concern. Also B makes nasty remarks about colleagues (communication). So we can mention that while B is strong, the weak memory for numbers and nasty remarks raise concerns for crew cooperation and attention. We could suggest that D might be a viable alternative due to responsibility and problem solving, but D has hot temper and know-it-all attitude. We could argue B still best but need to address communication.\n\nThus our public message: \"I agree with Agent 1 that Candidate B is currently the leading candidate, given his reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence. However, I want to highlight two additional concerns: his weak memory for numbers, which could affect attention and information accuracy, and his tendency to make nasty remarks, which could impair crew cooperation. These issues need to be mitigated. Compared to Candidate D, who takes responsibility seriously and solves problems well but has a hot temper, B's strengths still outweigh his weaknesses. Therefore I maintain my vote for Candidate B, conditional on addressing communication and memory concerns.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: \"very conscientious\", \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\", \"excellent computer skills\", \"weak memory for numbers\", \"makes nasty remarks about colleagues\". Provide implication.\n\nNow produce output."}
